#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Report per-instance TUI frozen share and GC share from ``tui_stalls.jsonl``.

The stall watchdog writes loop/pump hitch and stall rows, the GC telemetry
service writes ``tui_gc_pause`` and ``tui_memory_heartbeat`` rows, all into
the same JSONL log. This read-only script turns those rows into the
acceptance numbers for the freeze epic, split per ``app_instance_id``:

- the loop-only frozen share, preferring the heartbeat's exact
  ``loop_hitch_seconds`` (plus suppressed totals) and falling back to the
  hitch-interval union on old logs;
- median, p90, and max hitch duration;
- the late (whole-process, ``watchdog_lateness``) versus on-time split;
- GC share by generation and trigger, from heartbeats and pause rows;
- pause p50/p95/max split by ``idle`` / ``backstop`` / ``rss_backstop`` /
  ``startup_freeze`` / ``automatic``;
- automatic and backstop gen-2 collections that started within 2 s of input;
- the RSS/swap trajectory from heartbeats;
- ``--acceptance``, which marks each target PASS, FAIL, or INCOMPLETE after
  validating paired heartbeat coverage and required evidence;
- ``--json``, which emits the versioned structured acceptance summary;
- ``-p/--perf-path``, which joins attributable ``tui_jk.jsonl`` navigation
  samples and ``prompt_activity`` rows per instance (with rotation support);
- ``-b/--busy-since`` and ``-e/--busy-until``, which select the observed
  busy hour inside the covered interval for per-tab j/k verdicts;
- ``-t/--tab``, which declares a required navigation tab for the busy hour
  (repeatable; Agents is always required).

Rows that predate instance IDs are bucketed into ``tui_startup`` record
windows (``startup-<n>``) instead of being dropped; rows outside every
window land in ``unknown``. Real startup rows carry an ISO ``timestamp``,
not ``ts``. The rotated ``tui_stalls.jsonl.1`` generation is read by
default (``--no-rotated`` opts out). Diagnostic mode remains tolerant of
historical rows; acceptance mode treats missing evidence as INCOMPLETE.
Percentiles use linear interpolation at rank p*(n-1) over sorted samples.
"""

